    <statement><p>Suppose that 592 ft of fencing are used to enclose a corral in the shape of a rectangle with a semicircle whose diameter is a side of the rectangle as the following figure:</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__WHFreeman__Rogawski_Calculus_Early_Transcendentals_Second_Edition__4_Applications_of_the_Derivative__4_7_Applied_Optimization__4_7_7_pg-image-1.png" width="33%">
<shortdescription>A semicircle of diameter x on top of a rectangle of length x and height y.</shortdescription>
</image>
<p>Find the dimensions of the corral with maximum area.</p>
<p><m>x =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> ft.</p>
<p><m>y =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/> ft.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>165.789349439421</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>82.8946747197105</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>From the picture, we see that <m>x</m> is the width of the corral, and therefore the diameter of the semicircle,</p>
<p>and that <m>y</m> is the height of the rectangular section. Thus the perimeter of the corral can be expressed</p>
<p>by the equation <m>2y+ x+ \frac{\pi}{2}x= 2y + (1+ \frac{\pi}{2})x= 592</m> ft or equivalently,</p>
<p><m>y=\frac{1}{2}(592 - (1+ \frac{\pi}{2})x)</m>. Since <m>x</m> and <m>y</m> must both be nonnegative, it follows that <m>x</m> must</p>
<p>be restricted to the interval <m>[0, \frac{592}{1+ \pi/2}]</m>. The area of the corral is the sum of the area of the</p>
<p>rectangle and semicircle, <m>A= xy + \frac{\pi}{8}x^2</m>. Making the substitution for <m>y</m> from the</p>
<p>constraint equation,</p>
<p><m>A(x)=\frac{1}{2}x(592 - (1+ \frac{\pi}{2})x) + \frac{\pi}{8}x^2 = 296 x - \frac{1}{2}(1+ \frac{\pi}{2})x^2 + \frac{\pi}{8}x^2</m>.</p>
<p>Now, <m>A'(x) = 296 - (1 + \frac{\pi}{2})x + \frac{\pi}{4}x = 0</m> implies <m>x= \frac{296}{(1+ \frac{\pi}{4})} \approx 165.789349439421</m>.</p>
<p>With <m>A(0)=0</m>,</p>
<p><m>A(\frac{296}{(1+ \frac{\pi}{4})}) \approx 24536.8237170343 \qquad</m> and <m>\qquad A(\frac{592}{1+ \frac{\pi}{2}}) \approx 20824.1823330573</m>,</p>
<p>it follows that the corral of maximum area has dimentions</p>
<p><m>x= \frac{296}{1+ \frac{\pi}{4}} \qquad</m> and <m>\qquad y= \frac{1}{2}(592 - (1+ \frac{\pi}{2}) \frac{296}{1+ \frac{\pi}{4}}) \approx 82.8946747197105</m>.</p>
</solution>
